course: dictionary
lesson: 12558
title: Devotion: love, loyalty and hard work
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Devotion is a noun with three main meanings: great love and loyalty to someone or something; giving a lot of time and effort to a job, hobby or cause; and, in church life, prayer and worship.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. «The dog waited at the gate every day, showing great devotion to its owner» is about love and loyalty. «Ben practised the violin every evening with devotion» is about hard work. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: The plural, devotions, means short prayers or a time of prayer. «Every morning the family had devotions together before breakfast» means they prayed or read the Bible together.
fact: Devotion means great love and loyalty, hard work for a cause, or prayer and worship.
fact: «Devotion» praises someone for faithful love or hard work.
fact: «Devotion to duty» means always doing your job well and faithfully.
fact: «Devotions» means short prayers or a time of prayer.
fact: Swap check: put «loyalty», «effort» or «prayer» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The dog waited by the gate every day, showing great devotion to its owner.» What does devotion mean here? | A loud bark | *Great love and loyalty | Fear of strangers | A new collar
exercise: Ben practised the violin for an hour every day. His teacher said, «You play with real devotion.» What does this praise? | Being too lazy to practise | Winning a prize | *Hard work and a lot of effort | Playing a song that is very old
exercise: «Every morning the family had devotions together before breakfast.» What are devotions here? | *Short prayers and a time of prayer | A breakfast of toast and jam | Shopping trips | Morning football games
test: «Her devotion to her family never faded, even when times were hard.» Which word is closest in meaning to devotion? | *Loyalty | Anger | Laziness | Boredom
test: «Tom showed devotion to his football team by training every day.» What does devotion mean here? | *Giving a lot of time and effort | Being afraid of the ball | Sleeping late | Losing interest in the game
exam: Jade reads, «Their devotion to the cause led them to raise money for years.» What does devotion suggest? | Ignoring the cause | Stopping early | Sadness | *Strong loyalty and effort for a cause
